# W1: the four-seat hang proof. c2-packed-tp4-warm4-diag = production's recipe with the in-trace sampler OFF (audits off, the production tail caps) and the request-width warm ON
# (QWEN_FAST_M3_REQUEST_WARM=1: widths 1, 2, 4 before the single block's capture), the hang instruments on and the stall watch at 120 s steps and 150 s builds.
# The same run is repeated five consecutive times on this image (W1, W1b-W1e): five completions are the proof. A stall restarts the count of five only on a new image.
# W pass (every W run): the warm line ('[PINDIAG] request widths warmed before the packed traces') comes BEFORE the '[PINDIAG] verify t1 engaged site=packed_verify' line with programs
# above 0; no [STALL] dump; every user at budget; the concurrent4_steady and steady_resend builds complete; c2_smoke_check is clean with 0 late prefill programs; no handle-guard reuse on the
# model or sampler CCL. Record request_warm_programs, request_warm_ms and first_engine_programs (expected about the control's less the warm's: at eight seats 132 against 238), the 'dram after attach'
# line (within about 1 MB of W2) and the census 'seq=1 ccl before/after' and each engine's rows=2 warm-up handles (expected flipped against W2 under the plain warm).
# Smoke tests: the S8-0 hang shapes (concurrent4_steady, steady_resend, replay_concurrent4) plus v172's sequence (concurrent4 -> concurrent4_steady) and S0t's (-> concurrent4_code_equal).
# Stop rule: any W1-series stall, a missing or late warm line, a warm with 0 programs or an attach refusal naming the flag stops the series; skip G and T, run W2 and W3 by hand if not yet run, then H1.
# Read the W1 stack on a stall: verifier_engine.py:291 (the rows=2 warm-up fence) = the class is not cured at four seats, next discriminator is the existing rshard arm; a drafter site (dflash_device,
# the proposal capture, publish_prewarm) = the class holds and the next code step is a request-drafter warm; elsewhere = record it.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-20 min; the tests 10-20 min: 25-40 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/warm4 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/warm4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or
# a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a is a PLACEHOLDER for ONE FRESH tag, built by B0 from the pushed tp4/warm4 commit; the driver
# substitutes it in every template once the image is built. A later commit needs a new tag.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-warm4-diag
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
